{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/footnote","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"footnote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFormattedText","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV8footnoteAA16MXLFormattedTextVSgvp","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"footnote"},"abstract":[{"text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/footnote"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"footnote","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFormattedText","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLFormattedTextV","text":"MXLFormattedText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<footnote>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}],"title":"MXLBarline","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline/footnote":{"title":"footnote","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/footnote","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":